From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vpu: the wait for a pending instance ends

An encoder setup that failed (VPU_EncGetInitialInfo) left its instance
marked pending on the core. VPU_WaitPendingInst then waited for that mark
to go in a loop with no sleep and no end: closing the channel kept a CPU
busy in the kernel for good, and nothing could use the core.

A failed setup now clears the mark. The wait returns at once when the
pending instance is the caller itself, sleeps between looks, and after
2 s takes the core over with an error message: a mark that stays that
long belongs to a command that ended without clearing it.

---
--- a/interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/vcodec/vpuapi/vpuapi.c
+++ b/interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/vcodec/vpuapi/vpuapi.c
@@ -3076,11 +3076,27 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/* How long an instance waits for another one's command on the same core. */
+#define VPU_PENDING_WAIT_MS 2000
+
+/* Waits until no other instance has a command pending on the core, then marks
+ * this one pending. An instance that is pending itself goes on: it waited
+ * already (a failed command can leave its mark). Another instance's mark that
+ * stays VPU_PENDING_WAIT_MS belongs to a command that ended without clearing
+ * it; the core is taken over then, rather than waiting forever in the
+ * kernel with the CPU busy. */
 static void VPU_WaitPendingInst(CodecInst *pCodecInst)
 {
-RETRY:
-	if (GetPendingInst(pCodecInst->coreIdx)) {
-		goto RETRY;
+	const unsigned long deadline = jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(VPU_PENDING_WAIT_MS);
+	CodecInst *pending;
+
+	while ((pending = GetPendingInst(pCodecInst->coreIdx)) && pending != pCodecInst) {
+		if (time_after(jiffies, deadline)) {
+			CVI_VC_ERR("core %d: instance %d still pending after %d ms; taken over\n",
+				   pCodecInst->coreIdx, pending->instIndex, VPU_PENDING_WAIT_MS);
+			break;
+		}
+		usleep_range(500, 1000);
 	}
 
 	SetPendingInst(pCodecInst->coreIdx, pCodecInst, __func__, __LINE__);
@@ -3212,6 +3228,8 @@
 	ret = ProductVpuEncSetup(pCodecInst);
 	if (ret != RETCODE_SUCCESS) {
 		CVI_VC_ERR("ProductVpuEncSetup ret error %d\n", ret);
+		/* No command of this instance runs any more. */
+		SetPendingInst(pCodecInst->coreIdx, NULL, __func__, __LINE__);
 		return ret;
 	}
 
